From 33f76507e77d186981026a32063d7ae756ae9a94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:52:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-54: spacing snaplines -- 8 px from a neighbour on
 the same row / column, a blue line (0.54.0)

WinForms / WPF show a blue snapline when a control is at the standard
distance from its neighbour. Now so does the design surface: while moving
or resizing, when the edge that faces a neighbour on the same row (or
column) comes within 5 px of 8 px from it (8 = BCB6's grid step), it lands
exactly 8 px away and a short blue line is drawn across the gap. The nearer
of an edge line (red, as before) and a spacing line wins.

Also: a group move no longer snaps to the old places of the other moving
members (snapLines skips them).

Test: probe (the Save button dragged to 2 px short of 8 px before sbtExit ->
exactly 8 px, the blue line 8 px long while dragging, gone after).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
